WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Have you heard of New Coke? It’s, like,&nbsp;
the 1980s and Coca-Cola is losing market&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.580
share to their rival, Pepsi. People like&nbsp;
Pepsi because it is sweeter. So they did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.340
something kind of crazy. They changed&nbsp;
their formula, their big secret formula,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.880
they changed it to make it more sweet and they&nbsp;
did a bunch of corporate research that came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.540
back and it was like, “Yeah, people like this&nbsp;
more. More than Pepsi and more than regular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:25.080
Coke.” [Ad] We gave America a choice and more&nbsp;
people said Coke is it. [Ad Song] It’s a hit!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:30.480
So in 1985, they tell the world that they&nbsp;
are releasing this new formula and because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:36.060
people are people, they lost their collective shit&nbsp;
about it, there were little protest groups. “Our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:41.940
children will never know refreshment.” So yeah,&nbsp;
there was huge backlash and after just 79 days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.380
Coca-Cola announced that they were bringing back&nbsp;
the old Coke and it would be called Coca-Cola&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:51.060
Classic so that everyone knew this wasn't New&nbsp;
Coke. And lo and behold, Coca-Cola started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.900
overtaking Pepsi again to become the most popular&nbsp;
sugary drink in the world. Congratulations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.100
Coca-Cola. I kind of am curious what new Coke&nbsp;
tastes like, but I guess I'll never know.

